+training and validation sets using the :py:func:`sklearn.model_selection.train_test_split`
+function from the `sklearn` library. Reserve separate data if you also need an independent
+final evaluation.
+
+For cross validation, split each outer training fold again to obtain an early-stopping
+validation set. Use the outer test fold only for scoring, not for choosing the stopping
+iteration. Different folds can select different numbers of trees; each outer score
+evaluates the same training procedure on different data. The following example uses
+fixed hyperparameters. If you use cross-validation results to select hyperparameters,
+those results are model-selection scores; a further held-out test set or nested cross
+validation is needed for an independent final evaluation.
 
